<title>UK: GEC eyes other defense deals - report.</title>
<headline>GEC eyes other defense deals - report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's General Electric Co Plc is looking at possible defence link-ups with French, German or Italian companies after France brought a halt to the sale of Thomson SA, the Wall Street Journal Europe newspaper reported on Monday.</p>
<p>GEC said it would have preferred to link up with Thomson, which was due to be sold to Lagardere Group until the deal was blocked by the French government last week. George Simpson, GEC chief executive, said that move was &quot;slowing&quot; up the consolidation process for the European defence industry.</p>
</text>
